Fillet: a tangent ride between two crossings whose rider is a closed
contour (mitcad#1926, after 1724).

A plate whose corners are rounded in plan, its top's rim rounded with 1
all round (one closed, tangent contour), past whose back edge a tower of
half a cylinder stands (2.3 or 2.5 from it at its apex), the tower's foot
rounded with 2: 1724 refused the closed rider (a walk over a part of a
periodic spine wrote past the spine's law arrays), and OCCT failed (the
blends intersecting).

- ChFi3d_Builder::RideOnBlendBetweenCrossings: a closed rider is walked on
  the larger blend's surface by a stripe of its own whose spine is the
  rider's edge beside the two crossings alone (an open spine of one edge,
  the rider's radius and concavity); that stripe is registered as the
  tangent ride for the walk (StartSolOverflow finds the support) and
  dropped after it. The walked piece's spine parameters are shifted to the
  rider's (its lines keep their own parameters; the pieces are split by
  those). The rider itself is not reset.
- The walk's range in the rider's spine parameters is measured on the
  spine's edge the two crossings project inside (Absc), not taken from the
  contact line's parameters: the line of an analytic blend starts on its
  own edge, so its parameters are the spine's on the spine's first edge
  only. An open rider of one edge, or whose crossings lie beside two
  edges, keeps the line's parameters as before.

